// expect: 9
// residual: free
// A DECLARED anonymous rest, reached by a call that proves the whole set at
// the SITE while the decl's own row stays honestly unknown.
//
// This fixture was banked at 7 — the wrong slot — then at 9-with-an-assumed
// mark, and both readings were era artifacts. The 7 was the offset taken from
// the known set's own ordering. The "assumed" mark was manufactured:
// absorb_into_residual wrote `[] assumed` onto cells that knew nothing, so
// pick's own decl row rendered as a guess because a guess had been written on
// it. With that write gone and free_in_ty no longer calling a BOUND row free,
// the call's proof reaches pick and the residual projects as what it is.
//
// There is no assumed twin to bank beside it, because since 2026-09-28 there
// is no assumed remainder: two open rows that meet each learn what the other
// knew and continue at ONE fresh variable for what neither has seen, so an
// unproven remainder is always a variable and projects open. The file keeps
// its name for the ledger entries that cite it.
fn pick(u: {zeta: Int, ...}) = u.zeta

fn main(q) = pick({alpha: 7, zeta: 9})
